Burkina Faso is mourning it's dead in  the barracks and Eerie silence only  broken by the names of soldiers  all killed by isil Fighters while  protecting a humanitarian Convoy in the  north last month it was when attacked  too many for military leader Ibrahim  trari angered by another humiliating  defeat he staged the coup last Friday  becoming Burkina faso's newest leader  the aftermath of the attack was captured  on mobile phone hundreds of trucks burnt  they were transporting wheat and rice to  Jibo a town of 350 000 people in the  north besieged by isil since February  where people are dying of hunger truck  driver Abdul wahab swadugar survived the  attack he's still in shock  during the attack we noticed our  soldiers were no match they were weaker  the isil fighters were stronger than us  whoever dared to face them were killed  on the spot  two million people are on the Move  fleeing the violence in the north  terrorists tell us to leave our village  our soldiers that are meant to protect  us are not able to kill them terrorists  have come to which a war there will be  no survivors  in the capital wagadugu people are  taking matters in their own hands  collecting food and clothes they will  hand over to the military which plans to  airdrop help for the besieged city of  Jibo  we heard that the Army sent 70 tons of  supplies considering how densely  populated Jibo is 70 tons is nothing  it's not enough we need to do more  it is a war Burkina Faso cannot afford  to lose explained trout rate to  diplomats and a visiting delegation from  the West African Regional body ecowas  the Army has lost control of nearly half  of the country  faced with setbacks commanding officers  appear divided on which military  strategy to adopt the young Captain will  have to rebuild trust in the ranks  command Alder and battle hardened  officers many of whom are frustrated and  unite a fragmented Army that has  suffered too many losses on the  Battlefront Nicholas Hawk Al Jazeera
 

